course: dictionary
lesson: 10000
title: Telephone: a machine and an action
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A telephone is a machine for talking to someone far away. «A telephone turns sound into a changing electric current and turns it back into sound at the other end.» Your voice travels along a wire or through the air, and the other person hears it come out of their phone.
explain: Telephone can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, it is the machine, and a telephone number is the number you dial to reach someone. As a verb, to telephone someone means to call them. «Please telephone me when you get home» means please call me. Phone is a short form that people use every day.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is right. «Please answer the telephone» means the phone is ringing and someone needs to pick it up. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: if «call» fits, the word is a verb.
fact: Telephone can be a noun (the machine) or a verb (to call someone).
fact: Phone is a short form of telephone, and it is the everyday word.
fact: Alexander Graham Bell is credited with the telephone, which he made in the 1870s.
fact: Useful phrases: «on the telephone», «mobile phone», «telephone box».
fact: Emergency numbers differ by country: 911 in the USA and Canada, 999 or 112 in the UK and Ireland, 000 in Australia, 111 in New Zealand. Call only in a real emergency, say your address and stay on the line.
exercise: «A telephone turns sound into a changing electric current.» What does a telephone turn sound into? | Smoke | Light | Paper letters | *A changing electric current
exercise: Mum says, «I will telephone Gran tonight.» What does telephone mean here? | To ring a bell in the house | *To call someone on the phone | To cook a meal | To write a letter
exercise: «Please write your telephone number on the form.» What is a telephone number? | *The number you dial to reach someone | The number of stairs in a house | The price of a phone | The time of day
test: Which is a short everyday form of telephone? | Teller | Telly | Telegraph | *Phone
test: In the USA, which number do you dial in an emergency? | 111 | 000 | 999 | *911
exam: In «Please telephone me when you get home», what kind of word is telephone? | An adjective | A number | *A verb, an action word for calling | A noun, the name of a machine
